  "slug": "metabolic-trait-robustness-microbial-e869",
  "summary": "New benchmarks test temporal and interventional causal discovery on simulated kinetic and CRISPR perturbation data, exposing partial-observability limits.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is systematic benchmarking of causal discovery for biological networks rather than new algorithm development. One preprint evaluates tMIIC, PCMCI+/LPCMCI and SVAR-FCI on simulated biochemical kinetic models, contrasting fully observed settings with partially observed ones containing latent confounders and unobserved variables. A published study compares interventional causal structure learning algorithms on synthetic and CRISPR perturbation data for gene regulatory network inference. Together they probe how temporal and interventional information affect recovery of causal structure. Three other preprints (BI-SCUDO Regression, DeepCINET, siGMA) address noise-aware or rank-based prediction from omics and screening data; they relate through noise handling but do not benchmark causal network inference.",
